@{
    ViewData["Title"] = T("Terms of Service") + " — DashLane";
    Layout = "_AuthLayout";
}

<div class="legal-page has-toc">
    <aside class="legal-toc" data-toc aria-label="@T("On this page")"><p>@T("On this page")</p><ol></ol></aside>

    <article class="legal-card">
        <p class="legal-kicker">DashLane Mobility</p>
        <h1 class="legal-title">@T("Terms of Service")</h1>
        <p class="legal-updated">@T("Last updated: November 10, 2026")</p>
        @if (IsFrench)
        {
            <p class="notice legal-lang-note">@T("This document is currently available in English only.")</p>
        }
        <p class="legal-lead">
            These terms describe how you may use the DashLane account and onboarding screens that are available today.
            Features that are not built yet, such as ride search, booking, payments, and messaging, are not covered as working services.
        </p>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>1. Acceptance</h2>
            <p>
                By creating an account or continuing to use DashLane, you agree to these Terms of Service and the
                <a class="legal-inline-link" href="@Url.Action("Privacy", "Home")">Privacy Policy</a>.
                If you do not agree, do not create an account.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>2. Eligibility</h2>
            <p>
                You must be at least 18 years old. During onboarding you provide a date of birth so DashLane can check that age requirement.
                You must provide accurate account information and keep it current.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>3. Accounts</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>You are responsible for the email and password you use to sign in.</li>
                <li>Passwords are stored as irreversible hashes. DashLane does not store your password in plain text.</li>
                <li>Do not share your account. Tell us if you believe someone else can access it.</li>
                <li>Google sign-in is available when Google OAuth client credentials are configured for the app.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>4. Onboarding and identity checks</h2>
            <p>
                Before booking or posting rides is available, DashLane asks you to complete profile steps that may include:
            </p>
            <ul>
                <li>Legal name, date of birth, gender, home city, and preferred language</li>
                <li>A profile photo, bio, languages, and travel preferences</li>
                <li>A phone number and a verification code</li>
                <li>A government document upload for identity review</li>
            </ul>
            <p>
                Verification codes are generated and sent by SMS through Twilio Verify and are never shown on screen.
                When automatic ID checks are enabled, a photo of your document is sent to ID Analyzer, which reads it and compares it with the name and date of birth you entered.
                Document files are stored with your account and are not shown on a public profile.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>5. Acceptable use</h2>
            <ul>
                <li>Use DashLane only for lawful purposes.</li>
                <li>Do not upload false identity documents or pretend to be someone else.</li>
                <li>Do not attempt to access another member’s account, files, or data.</li>
                <li>Do not abuse, harass, or threaten other members when ride features become available.</li>
            </ul>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>6. Services that are not available yet</h2>
            <p>
                The ride feed, booking, payments, driver posting, live messaging, insurance, and call or SMS relays between members are not available in this build.
                Finishing onboarding saves your profile; it does not unlock a marketplace that has not been built.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>7. Local development storage</h2>
            <p>
                This application currently stores member accounts in a local SQLite database on the machine running the server.
                Treat that environment as a development or demonstration system unless you deploy it under your own hosting and legal review.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>8. Suspension</h2>
            <p>
                DashLane may refuse, suspend, or delete an account that provides false information, uploads abusive content, or violates these terms.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>9. Disclaimer</h2>
            <p>
                DashLane is provided as-is for the features that exist today. We do not promise uninterrupted service, availability of future ride features, or third-party certifications that are not implemented.
            </p>
        </section>

        <section class="legal-section">
            <h2>10. Contact</h2>
            <p>
                Questions about these terms can be raised through the product owner for this project until a public support channel is published.
            </p>
        </section>

        <nav class="legal-nav" aria-label="Related policies">
            <a class="legal-nav-link" href="@Url.Action("Privacy", "Home")">@T("Privacy Policy")</a>
            <a class="legal-nav-link" href="@Url.Action("SecurityWhitepaper", "Home")">@T("Security Whitepaper")</a>
            <a class="legal-nav-link" href="@Url.Action("Index", "Home")">@T("Back to welcome")</a>
        </nav>
    </article>
</div>
